window.MONSTER_CHUNK_152 = [{"name":"Elemental Earth Dragon","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":26,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+18 natural, -2 size","hp":252,"hd":"24d10+120","hdvalue":24,"fort":13,"ref":14,"will":15,"defensive_abilities":["earth mastery"],"dr":"10/magic and cold iron","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"burrow","speed":20}],"melee":"bite +35 (2d8+18), 2 claws +35 (2d6+12), 2 wings +32 (1d8+12), tail slap +32 (2d6+18)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50 ft. cone, DC 29, 14d8 fire and slashing"}],"strength":35,"dexterity":10,"constitution":20,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":12,"charisma":10,"baseatk":24,"cmb":38,"cmd":48,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (breath weapon)"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":19},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":27},{"skill":"Perception","value":28},{"skill":"Survival","value":28}],"languages":["Common","Terran"],"sq":[{"type":"assimilation"},{"type":"freeze"},{"type":"meld with stone"}],"environments":["any (Plane of Earth)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature resembles a 30-foot long dragon composed of stone and earth. Its great wings glisten like polished stone. Its eyes are deep gray and its roar seems to shake the very earth itself.","group":"Elemental Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Assimilation","kind":"Su","details":"When an elemental earth dragon slays an opponent, it dehydrates the flesh with its breath weapon and pulverizes the bones. The residue is then absorbed into the dragon's body. An assimilated creature can only be restored to life using wish, miracle, or true resurrection, but even then, there is a 50% chance that such powerful magic fails."},{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"An elemental earth dragon's breath weapon is a 50 ft. cone of scorching sand and gravel."},{"type":"Earth Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"An elemental earth dragon gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls if both it and its foes are touching the ground. If an opponent is airborne or waterborne, the elemental earth dragon takes a -4 penalty on attack and damage rolls. (These modifiers are not included in the stat block.)"},{"type":"Freeze","kind":"Ex","details":"An elemental earth dragon can hold itself so still it appears to be a statue. An observer must succeed on a DC 20 Perception check to notice that the elemental earth dragon is really alive."},{"type":"Meld into Stone","kind":"Ex","details":"An elemental earth dragon can meld its body with any stone surface large enough to accommodate its entire body. This is a standard action and has an unlimited duration (the dragon can stay melded as long as it desires). It otherwise resembles the meld into stone spell (caster level 20th)."}],"description":"Elemental earth dragons are the strongest of the elemental dragons. Using their great stone tail or earthen claws, they can destroy almost anything in short order. The majority of their time is spent burrowing through the Plane of Earth devouring gems, minerals, and silicate life forms. On occasion, they are summoned to the Material Plane by evil (and foolish) spellcasters who usually live just long enough to regret their mistake. Elemental earth dragons are evil (perhaps the most evil of the elemental dragons in addition to being the strongest) and despise most other forms of life. They rarely associate with other creatures, though a few have been known to have dealings with the occasional earth elemental. Elemental earth dragons cannot enter water; they must burrow under it or walk around it. The average elemental earth dragon is 30 ft. long. Its roar can be heard up to 5 miles away. Elemental earth dragons prefer to attack from ambush and secret rather than using a direct frontal assault. An elemental earth dragon lies in wait using its freeze ability or meld into stone ability and springs to attack when its prey comes into range. They are also fond of burrowing into the ground and surfacing under their prey, thereby gaining total surprise. Slain opponents are processed and absorbed into the body of the elemental earth dragon.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mortuary Cyclone","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"undead","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["desecrating aura (50 ft.)"],"ac":28,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +15 natural, +4 profane, -2 size","hp":263,"hd":"31d8+124","hdvalue":31,"fort":20,"ref":17,"will":24,"dr":"15/bludgeoning and magic","immunities":["undead traits"],"sr":31,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"slam +33 (2d8+16/19-20 plus energy drain)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"create spawn"},{"type":"energy drain","details":"2 levels, DC 29"},{"type":"necrocone"},{"type":"whirlwind","details":"10-40 ft. high, 3d6 damage, DC 36"}],"strength":33,"dexterity":12,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":12,"charisma":19,"baseatk":23,"cmb":36,"cmd":49,"feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (energy drain)"},{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (slam)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Iron Will"},{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Intimidate)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":32},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":46},{"skill":"Perception","value":39},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":1},{"skill":"Stealth","value":27}],"languages":["Common (cannot speak)"],"sq":[{"type":"unholy grace"}],"environments":["any land"],"organizations":["solitary","band (10-40 HD of undead creatures)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A whirling and spinning cyclone of dirt, bone fragments, and body parts rapidly advances toward you. It stands about 20 ft. tall. From its central form you see two large arm-like appendages ending in clench fists emerge.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Create Spawn","kind":"Su","details":"Any living creature slain by a mortuary cyclone's necrocone attack or energy drain attack becomes an undead creature in 1d4 rounds. Spawn are under the command of the mortuary cyclone that created them and remain enslaved until its destruction."},{"type":"Desecrating Aura","kind":"Su","details":"A mortuary cyclone emanates an aura of desecration within a 50-foot radius centered on its body. This functions as a desecrate spell (caster level 18th) as if the mortuary cyclone where a permanent fixture dedicated to its own deity. Clerics in the area take a -6 profane penalty on turning checks, undead within the area gain a +2 profane bonus on attack rolls, damage rolls, and saves, and undead created within the area have +2 hit points per HD. Further, anyone casting animate dead within 50 ft. of a mortuary cyclone creates as many as double the normal amount of undead (4 HD per caster level instead of 2 HD per caster level). A consecrate spell cast on a mortuary cyclone by a caster of 18th level or higher nullifies its desecrating aura for 1 minute per caster level."},{"type":"Necrocone","kind":"Su","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds, a mortuary cyclone can blast forth a mass of bone fragments, debris and negative energy in a 30-foot cone. Creatures caught in the cone take 6d6 points of damage. Half this damage is piercing damage, but the other half is from negative energy and isn't subject to resistance or immunity (unless the opponent is resistant or immune to negative energy effects). An affected creature that succeeds on a DC 27 Reflex save reduces the piercing damage by half. Undead within the area of a necrocone heal a number of hit points equal to the amount of negative energy damage (3d6) the attack would otherwise deal. An undead creature cannot gain temporary or bonus hit points from a mortuary cyclone's necrocone. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Unholy Grace","kind":"Su","details":"A mortuary cyclone adds its Charisma modifier as a bonus on its saving throws and as a profane bonus to its Armor Class. (The statistics block already reflects these bonuses.)"}],"description":"A mortuary cyclone is an undead creature born when living creatures tamper with or desecrate a mass grave (either magically or naturally).\n\nThough not evil by nature, the destruction a mortuary cyclone deals and leaves in its wake is legendary. These creatures simply decide on a direction to move, and much like a natural occurring tornado, they move in that direction without regard to who or what stands in their way. A single mortuary cyclone is more than capable of destroying a village or small town in a very short time if left unchecked.\n\nA mortuary cyclone appears as a 20 foot tall or taller tornado composed of grave dirt, bone fragments, and body parts all swirling around in its whirlwind form.\n\nMortuary cyclones feed on the energy of living creatures. Such creatures caught in the path of a mortuary cyclone are sucked into its central form and pummeled by high speed winds, bone fragments, and negative energy. Slain creatures are deposited on the ground where they rise as undead \"slaves\" in command of the mortuary cyclone.\n\nA mortuary cyclone attacks by forming pseudo-fists from its whirlwind form and pummeling its foes or by absorbing them into its whirlwind (its favored method of attack). A mortuary cyclone simply has to move into a creature's space to pull it into it cyclonic form. It continues raining its fists down on creatures that avoid its whirlwind, all the while, firing a burst of bone fragments and negative energy at foes attempting to keep their distance.\n\nA mortuary cyclone's natural weapons are treated as magic weapons for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.\n\nMortuary Cyclone Spawn A creature killed by a mortuary cyclone's necrocone rises as an undead creature in 1d4 rounds. The type is based on the creature's total HD.\n\nTotal HD Opponent Rises as Less than 10 Zombie or skeleton 11-15 HD Wraith 16-20 HD Spectre 21+ HD Dread wraith.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Quantum","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"aberration","subtypes":["extraplanar"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":32,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+3 deflection, +4 Dex, +17 natural, -2 size","hp":357,"hd":"34d8+170 (+34)","hdvalue":34,"fort":18,"ref":17,"will":23,"defensive_abilities":["unstable form"],"dr":"15/adamantine","speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":40,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"5 tentacles +34 (2d6+11)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"disintegration"}],"strength":33,"dexterity":18,"constitution":21,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":14,"charisma":17,"baseatk":25,"cmb":38,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. bull rush","cmd":55,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. bull rush can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Greater Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Stand Still"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":41},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":37},{"skill":"Perception","value":47},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":43}],"languages":["Common","Quantum"],"sq":[{"type":"quantum form"},{"type":"quantum movement"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature seems to have no true shape, as its outline flickers and changes seemingly at random. At first it appears to have four tentacles, then in a flicker eight more appear and waver menacingly before shimmering once more out of existence. Its general shape is serpentine, with an uncertain number of tentacles dangling beneath it, but the only constants are its six glowing eyes, three on each side of what must be its head.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Disintegration","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day, as a full-round action, a quantum can attack with a single tentacle. If it hits, it sets up subatomic vibrations that shake apart the molecular structure of its opponent. The target must succeed on a DC 32 Fortitude save or take 40d6 points of damage. Even if the save succeeds, the target takes 10d6 points of damage. This effect functions as a disintegrate spell (CL 34th). A quantum can use this ability when it uses its quantum form. Each use by one of its forms counts against its daily use limit. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Quantum Form","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day and once per round, a quantum can move in such a way as to appear in two places at once, at a distance no greater than 30 ft. This is a free action that provokes an attack of opportunity and lasts only one round. While occupying two spaces simultaneously, each representation of the quantum can perform one independent standard action (including using the quantum's special attacks). Using this ability, the same quantum could attack two different opponents, or attack one opponent while opening a door to escape, and so on. At the end of the round, both instances of the quantum return to the space it originally occupied before activating this ability."},{"type":"Quantum Movement","kind":"Su","details":"At will a quantum can use the dimension door spell as a standard action (CL 34th)."},{"type":"Unstable Form","kind":"Su","details":"A quantum has a deflection bonus to its Armor Class equal to its Charisma bonus. Further, because it moves by means of short-distance teleportation, attacks aimed at a quantum have a 20% miss chance."}],"description":"The quantums hail from beyond and between all planes. The first quantum is said to have followed a lost band of adventurers back after they became lost on a planar journey.\n\nA quantum exists simultaneously in many dimensions at once, which gives it a flickering, seemingly insubstantial shape as if some mad god is continually creating and re-creating it on a whim. If its form could somehow be stabilized into only three dimensions, a quantum would resemble a flattened jellyfish with a knob at the top containing six unblinking eyes. It has an oblong body with many tentacles radiating out from beneath its body. The exact number of tentacles cannot be known, however, since stabilizing a quantum's shape is a task yet to be undertaken and may not even be possible.\n\nQuantums move by avoiding space entirely. A quantum hovers like some eerie jellyfish but doesn't fly by conventional means. Instead a quantum actually teleports short distances too fast for the eye to detect and in this manner it appears to be hovering. A quantum can also teleport across greater distances. At one moment a quantum can be in one space and then in an instant it is somewhere else, having never been at any point between. The flickering form of a quantum allows it to attack with one tentacle, two, six, as many as it needs. Attack-capable limbs seem to manifest themselves as they are needed, then vanish again as if they had never existed.\n\nA quantum lashes out at its foes with its tentacles. Against a particularly powerful opponent, it uses its disintegration attack. When facing multiple foes, a quantum uses its quantum form to better its odds or make its escape.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Ravager Spawn","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":40,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":35,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +27 natural, -2 size","hp":495,"hd":"30d10+300 (+30)","hdvalue":30,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (epic-level weapons and artifacts)","vampiric healing"],"fort":29,"ref":22,"will":19,"defensive_abilities":["magic disruption (1 on d20)"],"dr":"15/epic","immunities":["energy drain"],"resists":[{"type":"death"},{"type":"energy","value":5}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":10}],"melee":"bite +37 (3d8+9/19-20/x3), 4 claws +37 (2d8+9/18-20)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","strength":28,"dexterity":20,"constitution":30,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":25,"charisma":18,"baseatk":30,"cmb":41,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","cmd":56,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Armor (x3)"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (claw)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":40}],"sq":[{"type":"form-shifting"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","brood (2-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This enormous creature stands 18 ft. high at the shoulders and has a body 30 ft. long. Its body is long and narrow, with eight stubby legs ending in ebon claws the size of large falchions. Its mouth is filled with sharp black teeth, and its eyes are jet-black orbs the size of dinner platters, set above a delicate muzzle like that of a bulldog. The body is hairless, covered with a thick, leathery crimson hide.","group":"Ravager","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Resistance","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn possesses an innate resistance to effects that would kill or permanently incapacitate it, including petrification and imprisonment. Against such effects it is considered to automatically make any required saving throws."},{"type":"Energy Resistance","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn possesses energy resistance against all forms of energy attack (fire, cold, electricity, acid, and sonic)."},{"type":"Form-Shifting","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn can physically alter its physiology to take on one of the three listed forms: the crawler, the brawler, or the flier. Doing so takes one minute, and during this period it cannot take any other actions, though it isn't considered helpless."},{"type":"Magic Disruption","kind":"Su","details":"Every time a Ravager spawn comes into contact with a spell or spell-like or supernatural effect, there is a chance as indicated above that the magic doesn't affect it. In the case of ongoing effects, a new check is made each round."},{"type":"Regeneration","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn treats all damage as subdual, except damage from epic-level weapons and artifacts."},{"type":"Vampiric Healing","kind":"Su","details":"Whenever a Ravager spawn hits with a melee attack, it is healed hit points equal to half the damage it inflicts on its opponent. This ability cannot heal it above its natural maximum hit points. This ability extends to its trample special attack, where applicable."}],"description":"The Ravager was created eons ago by a primeval race of beings who believed in the unity of three forces: body, mind, and spirit. In their ongoing war with another race of savages, they created several weapons of terrible power. The greatest of these is the living beast known only as the Ravager.\n\nThis beast was given incredible vitality, and the power to manipulate its own body to assume a form most advantageous to it: a crawling weasel-like form that can burrow, a hulking apelike humanoid form with greater reach and strength, and a winged form to allow it greater mobility and agility.\n\nAfter being used once or twice on the battlefield, those who created it realized its awesome danger and contained it in the strongest prison they could devise, suspended in time until it would once again be needed.\n\nHowever, due to the subsequent influence of Orcus near the vault where the Ravager was contained, the wards were damaged, and a taint of evil infected its quarantine. This has resulted in it reproducing asexually, and has granted the ravager an astonishing capacity for growth. For every week that it lives, it permanently gains 1 hit die. There is no known limit to how far this advancement can go before it either devastates the planet it lives on or collapses under its own weight.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk Reloaded (© Necromancer Games, 2006)"},{"name":"Ravager Spawn","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":37,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +24 natural, -2 size","hp":405,"hd":"30d10+210 (+30)","hdvalue":30,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (epic-level weapons and artifacts)","vampiric healing"],"fort":26,"ref":22,"will":19,"defensive_abilities":["magic disruption (1 on d20)"],"dr":"15/epic","immunities":["energy drain"],"resists":[{"type":"death"},{"type":"energy","value":5}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +40 (3d6+12/x3), 2 claws +40 (1d12+12/15-20)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","strength":34,"dexterity":20,"constitution":24,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":25,"charisma":18,"baseatk":30,"cmb":43,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","cmd":58,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Greater Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Staggering Critical"},{"feat":"Stunning Critical"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":40}],"sq":[{"type":"form-shifting"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","brood (2-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"Towering 35 ft. high is a massive, apelike creature, resting on two sets of powerfully muscled legs. A third set of arms, thick and corded with muscle, bulges out from its massive shoulders, ending with massive black claws. The mouth is filled with jagged black teeth, and glistening black eyes are set over a wide muzzle. Its skin is deep red, somewhat lighter on the underbelly.","group":"Ravager","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Resistance","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn possesses an innate resistance to effects that would kill or permanently incapacitate it, including petrification and imprisonment. Against such effects it is considered to automatically make any required saving throws."},{"type":"Energy Resistance","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn possesses energy resistance against all forms of energy attack (fire, cold, electricity, acid, and sonic)."},{"type":"Form-Shifting","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn can physically alter its physiology to take on one of the three listed forms: the crawler, the brawler, or the flier. Doing so takes one minute, and during this period it cannot take any other actions, though it isn't considered helpless."},{"type":"Magic Disruption","kind":"Su","details":"Every time a Ravager spawn comes into contact with a spell or spell-like or supernatural effect, there is a chance as indicated above that the magic doesn't affect it. In the case of ongoing effects, a new check is made each round."},{"type":"Regeneration","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn treats all damage as subdual, except damage from epic-level weapons and artifacts."},{"type":"Vampiric Healing","kind":"Su","details":"Whenever a Ravager spawn hits with a melee attack, it is healed hit points equal to half the damage it inflicts on its opponent. This ability cannot heal it above its natural maximum hit points. This ability extends to its trample special attack, where applicable."}],"description":"The Ravager was created eons ago by a primeval race of beings who believed in the unity of three forces: body, mind, and spirit. In their ongoing war with another race of savages, they created several weapons of terrible power. The greatest of these is the living beast known only as the Ravager.\n\nThis beast was given incredible vitality, and the power to manipulate its own body to assume a form most advantageous to it: a crawling weasel-like form that can burrow, a hulking apelike humanoid form with greater reach and strength, and a winged form to allow it greater mobility and agility.\n\nAfter being used once or twice on the battlefield, those who created it realized its awesome danger and contained it in the strongest prison they could devise, suspended in time until it would once again be needed.\n\nHowever, due to the subsequent influence of Orcus near the vault where the Ravager was contained, the wards were damaged, and a taint of evil infected its quarantine. This has resulted in it reproducing asexually, and has granted the ravager an astonishing capacity for growth. For every week that it lives, it permanently gains 1 hit die. There is no known limit to how far this advancement can go before it either devastates the planet it lives on or collapses under its own weight.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk Reloaded (© Necromancer Games, 2006)"},{"name":"Ravager Spawn","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":40,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+8 Dex, +24 natural, -2 size","hp":405,"hd":"30d10+210 (+30)","hdvalue":30,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (epic-level weapons and artifacts)","vampiric healing"],"fort":25,"ref":27,"will":19,"defensive_abilities":["magic disruption (1 on d20)"],"dr":"15/epic","immunities":["energy drain"],"resists":[{"type":"death"},{"type":"energy","value":5}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"bite +37 (3d6+9/x3), 2 claws +37 (1d12+9/18-20)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","strength":28,"dexterity":26,"constitution":24,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":25,"charisma":18,"baseatk":30,"cmb":41,"cmd":59,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Lunge"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Fly)"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Wingover"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":22},{"skill":"Perception","value":18}],"sq":[{"type":"form-shifting"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","brood (2-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"With a crack and boom, this creature spreads a pair of great leathery wings over 50 ft. in span. Its body is lean and covered with rippling muscle beneath a thick, leathery crimson hide. Its claws and teeth are black, as are its eyes.","group":"Ravager","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Resistance","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn possesses an innate resistance to effects that would kill or permanently incapacitate it, including petrification and imprisonment. Against such effects it is considered to automatically make any required saving throws."},{"type":"Energy Resistance","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn possesses energy resistance against all forms of energy attack (fire, cold, electricity, acid, and sonic)."},{"type":"Form-Shifting","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn can physically alter its physiology to take on one of the three listed forms: the crawler, the brawler, or the flier. Doing so takes one minute, and during this period it cannot take any other actions, though it isn't considered helpless."},{"type":"Magic Disruption","kind":"Su","details":"Every time a Ravager spawn comes into contact with a spell or spell-like or supernatural effect, there is a chance as indicated above that the magic doesn't affect it. In the case of ongoing effects, a new check is made each round."},{"type":"Regeneration","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn treats all damage as subdual, except damage from epic-level weapons and artifacts."},{"type":"Vampiric Healing","kind":"Su","details":"Whenever a Ravager spawn hits with a melee attack, it is healed hit points equal to half the damage it inflicts on its opponent. This ability cannot heal it above its natural maximum hit points. This ability extends to its trample special attack, where applicable."}],"description":"The Ravager was created eons ago by a primeval race of beings who believed in the unity of three forces: body, mind, and spirit. In their ongoing war with another race of savages, they created several weapons of terrible power. The greatest of these is the living beast known only as the Ravager.\n\nThis beast was given incredible vitality, and the power to manipulate its own body to assume a form most advantageous to it: a crawling weasel-like form that can burrow, a hulking apelike humanoid form with greater reach and strength, and a winged form to allow it greater mobility and agility.\n\nAfter being used once or twice on the battlefield, those who created it realized its awesome danger and contained it in the strongest prison they could devise, suspended in time until it would once again be needed.\n\nHowever, due to the subsequent influence of Orcus near the vault where the Ravager was contained, the wards were damaged, and a taint of evil infected its quarantine. This has resulted in it reproducing asexually, and has granted the ravager an astonishing capacity for growth. For every week that it lives, it permanently gains 1 hit die. There is no known limit to how far this advancement can go before it either devastates the planet it lives on or collapses under its own weight.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk Reloaded (© Necromancer Games, 2006)"},{"name":"Slag Worm","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Gargantuan","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar","fire"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["intense heat (10 ft., DC 30, 4d6 fire)"],"ac":36,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":34,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +28 natural, -4 size","hp":348,"hd":"24d10+192 (+24)","hdvalue":24,"fort":18,"ref":18,"will":20,"defensive_abilities":["fire absorption"],"dr":"15/adamantine","immunities":["fire","elemental traits"],"weaknesses":["susceptible to rust","vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"burrow","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +36 (6d10+22/19-20 plus grab)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"deafening roar"},{"type":"intense heat"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"4d6 plus 4d6 fire damage, AC 24, 34 hp"}],"strength":41,"dexterity":14,"constitution":26,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":19,"charisma":10,"baseatk":24,"cmb":43,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +4 vs. grapple","cmd":55,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":28},{"skill":"Bluff","value":27},{"skill":"Climb","value":39},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (engineering)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":31},{"skill":"Perception","value":35},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":35},{"skill":"Survival","value":31}],"languages":["Ignan","Terran"],"environments":["any (Elemental Plane of Earth)","any (Elemental Plane of Fire)","any (Plane of Molten Skies)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This massive wormlike creature of burnt iron and glistening hematite grinds with the roar of the forge. Its fanged lamprey like mouth opens to reveal the molten fires burning in its gut.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Deafening Roar","kind":"Su","details":"Whenever a slag worm moves at least half of its speed in a single round it creates a grinding roar of metal on metal from its body. Creatures within 50 ft. that hear this grinding roar must succeed on a DC 30 Fortitude save or be deafened for 2d4 rounds. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Intense Heat","kind":"Ex","details":"A slag worm's body generates intense heat. Anything within 10 ft. of its body takes 4d6 points of fire damage each round. A DC 30 Fortitude save reduces the damage by half. Any weapon that strikes a slag worm must succeed on a DC 30 Fortitude save or melt into slag. (Magic weapons gain their enhancement bonus to their save.) A creature striking a slag worm with a natural attack or unarmed takes the same 4d6 points of damage each time an attack hits. The save DCs are Constitution-based."},{"type":"Fire Absorption","kind":"Ex","details":"Fire deals no damage to a slag worm. Instead, the slag worm absorbs the effect and heals 1 point of damage for each 3 points the effect would otherwise deal. If the amount of healing would cause the slag worm to exceed its full normal hit points, it gains any excess as temporary hit points."},{"type":"Susceptible to Rust","kind":"Ex","details":"Attacks that cause rusting (such as a rusting grasp spell or the touch of a rust monster) deal 2d6 points of damage to a slag worm."}],"description":"Slag worms burrow endlessly through the elemental Plane of Earth, Elemental Plane of Fire, and Plane of Molten Skies, occasionally forcing through weak points into the material planes where they burrow deep beneath the earth, devouring raw iron deposits to keep their internal furnaces burning. Because of this they have been known to devour entire companies of heavily armored dwarves and orcs, mistaking their gear for a new vein of naturally occurring iron salts.\n\nSlag worms average about 40 ft. long and weigh about 60,000 pounds, though specimens as large as 100 ft. or more have been rumored to exist. Its massive form radiates abysmal heat and when the worm opens its maw, fires can be seen burning and raging in its interior. They are intelligent creatures (more so than their appearance of a big dumb worm would lead one to believe) and can speak though they rarely choose to converse with other races.\n\nA slag worm erupts from the ground seeking to eat anything wearing iron, steel, or other metal armor or equipment. It attacks such creatures with a great ferocity, generally disregarding other enemies until the worm is heavily injured or forced away by magic.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Sthenno","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":38,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":35,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +26 natural, -1 size","hp":225,"hd":"18d10+126","hdvalue":18,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":13,"ref":16,"will":17,"dr":"15/epic and good","immunities":["paralysis","polymorph","sleep","stunning"],"sr":31,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"2 claws +28 (2d6+10 plus grab), bite +28 (1d10+10),  snake bite +26 (1d8+5 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"petrifying gaze"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 2d6+15"}],"strength":31,"dexterity":17,"constitution":24,"intelligence":22,"wisdom":22,"charisma":26,"baseatk":18,"cmb":29,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":42,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (snake bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":24},{"skill":"Bluff","value":29},{"skill":"Craft (alchemy)","value":27},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":29},{"skill":"Fly","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":29},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":27},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":27},{"skill":"Stealth","value":20},{"skill":"Survival","value":24}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aklo","Common","Draconic","Infernal","Terran (Euryale only)","Undercommon"],"sq":[{"type":"immortal"}],"environments":["any (Outer Planes)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair (Sthenno and Euryale)","troupe (true gorgon plus 2-8 medusa and 1-4 greater medusa)"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"This hideous creature appears to be almost twice as tall as a normal human.  Its upper torso is that of a well proportioned human female with scaly flesh while its lower torso is that of a great black-scaled snake. Small black wings protrude from its back. Instead of hair, its head is covered with writhing, deadly asps. Its mouth is filled with razor-sharpened fangs.","group":"True Gorgon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Immortal","kind":"Ex","details":"Sthenno and Euryale are immortal and cannot die from natural causes. They are not subject to death from massive damage and are immune to death effects and disintegration. They don't age, and don't need to sleep, eat, or breathe."},{"type":"Petrifying Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Turn to stone permanently, 30 ft., Fortitude save (DC 27 Sthenno, DC 29 Euryale) negates. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 26 (Sthenno) or DC 28 (Euryale); frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d6 Strength; cure 1 save."}],"description":"Though the word gorgon is often associated with the deadly bull-like creature that turns a victim to stone with its breath weapon, the true gorgons are three sisters; Euryale, Sthenno, and Medusa. They are the daughters of the god Phorcys and the goddess Ceto. Euryale and Sthenno were born immortal and are hideous creatures with writing snakes for hair, brass claws, wings, and a gaze that can turn any living creature into stone. Phorcys tasked them with guarding the entrance to the Underworld.\n\nMedusa was born mortal and was very beautiful. Phorcys sent her to the Material Plane so all could gaze upon the beauty of his daughter.\n\nMedusa's beauty rivaled that of some of the goddesses, and some of them grew jealous of Medusa, particularly the goddess Athena. Her beauty also turned the heads of some of the gods, and when Poseidon seduced her in a temple to Athena, the goddess became enraged and changed the beautiful Medusa into a creature as hideous as her sisters. Poseidon turned from his love, never to return again. Medusa, enraged, fled into the desert and never came back to civilization.\n\nThe hero Perseus was tasked with killing the gorgon known as Medusa and bringing her head to King Polydectes as a wedding present. Using a magic shield given to him by the gods, he avoided Medusa's deadly gaze and severed her head. From her serpentine body sprang the children of Poseidon, creatures similar in appearance to their mother. These creatures escaped into the world and are called medusa.\n\nSthenno and Euryale long for their sister's return or their meeting with her in the Underworld. Yet being immortal, they cannot enter the Realm of the Dead. Thus, both know they will never see their beloved sibling again. Their cries are said to be audible on the wind as a high-pitched shrill akin to a bird's cry.\n\nBoth Sthenno and Euryale are 10 ft. tall and weigh around 600 pounds or more. Sthenno's eyes are blue; Euryale's eyes are copper.\n\nSthenno and Euryale rarely enter combat unless pressed or provoked.\n\nThey are both deadly combatants and use their claws, bite, snakes, and petrifying gaze with precision force. Sthenno enjoys \"collecting\" those she has turned to stone and even has a room in her lair where she displays them. Euryale simply smashes to rubble those she has petrified.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Titivilus","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":41,"ac_touch":28,"ac_flat_footed":34,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +13 natural, +11 profane","hp":275,"hd":"19d10+171","hdvalue":19,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":15,"ref":20,"will":2,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":31,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"+3 silver wounding longsword +29 (1d8+10/19-20 plus 1 bleed) or fear touch +26 (fear)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fear touch","details":"Will DC 32, fear spell CL 20th"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":29,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"bestow curse"},{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"confusion"},{"spell":"crushing despair"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"hypnotism"},{"spell":"illusory script"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"misdirection"},{"spell":"nondetection"},{"spell":"polymorph"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"unholy aura"},{"spell":"ventriloquism"},{"spell":"whispering wind"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"feeblemind"},{"spell":"symbol of pain"},{"spell":"symbol of sleep"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 lemures or nupperibos, 1d4 bone devils or erinyes, 1d2 horned devils, or 1 pit fiend 100%"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":24,"constitution":28,"intelligence":28,"wisdom":26,"charisma":32,"baseatk":19,"cmb":13,"cmd":26,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (confusion)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":28},{"skill":"Bluff","value":40},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":38},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":29},{"skill":"Fly","value":29},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":37},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":34},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":34},{"skill":"Stealth","value":29},{"skill":"Survival","value":30}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Daemonic","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Ignan","Infernal","Terran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Titivilus pls 2-4 erinyes or bearded devils)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This 6-foot tall creature resembles a satyr with a round hairless head, the lower torso of a goat, cloven ft., and clawed hands. Small black leathery wings sprout from his back. His eyes are the color of coal.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fear Touch","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by Titivilus's fear touch for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Titivilus the Confuser serves Lord Dispater as messenger and chamberlain. He is a very evil and malign duke. His ability to manipulate others is legendary throughout the Hells, and it is because of this gift that Dispater allows him to attend infernal meetings where dukes are normally prohibited.\n\nTitivilus spends most of his days in his tower, Martyr's Curse, a large structure composed of blackened iron. When encountered away from his tower he usually has a small retinue of bearded devils or erinyes with him.\n\nTitivilus stands 6 ft. tall and weighs 220 pounds.\n\nTitivilus prefers to avoid combat, if possible. If pressed, he attacks with his spell-like abilities, seeking to sew confusion and disorder among his adversaries. In close combat, he uses his longsword, but usually summons other devils before such combat occurs. If facing imminent defeat, Titivilus summons other devils to cover his escape.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Titivilus originally appeared in Dragon #75 (© TSR/ Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission.","gear":"+3 silver wounding longsword"},{"name":"Wrath Dragon","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"NG","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["extraplanar","good"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"scent"}],"auras":["magic circle against evil (10 ft. radius)"],"ac":30,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +20 natural, -2 size","hp":465,"hd":"30d12+270","hdvalue":30,"fort":26,"ref":19,"will":23,"dr":"15/evil","immunities":["fire","poison","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":29,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +37 (2d8+15), 2 claws +37 (2d6+10), 2 wings +34 (1d8+5), tail slap +34 (2d6+15)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50 ft. cone, DC 34, 20d6 fire"},{"type":"channel positive energy","details":"8/day, 8d6, DC 22"},{"type":"crush"},{"type":"holy lance","details":"2/day, 7 rounds"},{"type":"might of the gods","details":"+15, 15 rounds/day"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon devas","details":"level 9, 1d2 astral devas, or 1d4 movanic or monadic devas, 100% chance"}]},{"frequency":"7/day","spells":[{"spell":"strength surge","details":"+7 bonus"},{"spell":"touch of good","details":"+7 bonus"}]}],"spellsprepared_caster":"cleric","spellsprepared_caster_level":15,"spellsprepared_concentration":24,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":8,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"antimagic field"},{"spell":"clenched fist","type":"domain"}]},{"spell_level":7,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"destruction"},{"spell":"holy word","type":"domain"},{"spell":"repulsion"}]},{"spell_level":6,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"banishment"},{"spell":"blade barrier"},{"spell":"heal"},{"spell":"stoneskin","type":"domain"}]},{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"atonement"},{"spell":"break enchantment"},{"spell":"dispel evil","type":"domain"},{"spell":"greater command"},{"spell":"plane shift"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"death ward"},{"spell":"dimensional anchor"},{"spell":"discern lies"},{"spell":"dismissal"},{"spell":"divine power"},{"spell":"holy smite","type":"domain"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"blindness/deafness"},{"spell":"invisibility purge"},{"spell":"magic vestment","type":"domain"},{"spell":"remove curse"},{"spell":"remove disease"},{"spell":"searing light"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"aid","type":"domain"},{"spell":"align weapon"},{"spell":"augury"},{"spell":"consecrate"},{"spell":"enthrall"},{"spell":"silence"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"bless"},{"spell":"command"},{"spell":"divine favor"},{"spell":"enlarge person","type":"domain"},{"spell":"remove fear"},{"spell":"sanctuary"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"guidance"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"virtue"}]}],"spelldomains":"Good, Strength","strength":31,"dexterity":14,"constitution":28,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":18,"charisma":20,"baseatk":30,"cmb":44,"cmd":56,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alignment Channel"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Turn Undead"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":38},{"skill":"Fly","value":27},{"skill":"Heal","value":37},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":38},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":36},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":36},{"skill":"Perception","value":37},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":37},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":38}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Terran"],"environments":["any good-aligned plane"],"organizations":["solitary","band (1 wrath dragon plus 1d4 astral devas)"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"Beautiful and awesome to behold, this majestic dragon's skin glitters like precious metals and jewels, belying its unquestionable might and holy wrath.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A wrath dragon's breath weapon is a 50 ft. cone of holy fire. One-half of the damage is from divine force and isn't subject to fire resistance or fire immunity."},{"type":"Divine Power","kind":"Su","details":"A wrath dragon casts spells and channels positive energy as a good-aligned cleric. Its caster level is equal to half its Hit Dice. It has access to the Good and Strength domains and gains the domain power of each domain."}],"description":"These massive powerfully built specimens are formed from the ascension of slain good dragons into the heavenly orders. Given the opportunity to return, they serve as heralds of good-aligned deities sent to deliver divine judgment on infidels and sinners who have turned their back on the path of righteousness. A flight of wrath dragons over an offending city has often been cause to turn an entire civilization to prayer and piety. Wrath dragons never enter the Material Plane, inner planes, or other outer planes unless under orders from the deity they serve. When such orders are given, a wrath dragon completes its assignment to the best of its ability before returning to its home plane. A wrath dragon serves no one other than the deity that \"created\" it. It aids good-aligned creatures in time of need, but doesn't serve them or stay with them any longer than is required to give aid (unless its deific orders say otherwise). A wrath dragon never aids an evil creature under any circumstances, and if forced to do so by magical means, the dragon seeks atonement as soon as possible. A wrath dragon is 30 ft. long and weighs about 30,000 pounds. Its scales are silver or platinum and glitter under bright light. Its wings are silver-hued with a darker stripe running along the top portion. Its head, sitting atop its long serpentine neck, is long and angular and its eyes are seemingly made of sapphire. Two under-curved horns made of ivory jut from its head just behind its eyes. Wrath dragons start combat with use of their breath weapon and divine spells. They continue this tactic until pressed with missile fire, or magic that would force them to close in for melee attacks. In close combat, a wrath dragon attacks using a combination of its bite, claws, and spells. If pressed, or if the battle turns against it, a wrath dragon summons devas to its aid.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Baaphel","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":39,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":37,"ac_mods":"+9 armor, +2 Dex, +11 natural, +7 profane","hp":270,"hd":"20d10+160","hdvalue":20,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":14,"ref":19,"will":22,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":32,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30,"special":"40 ft. without armor"},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"special":"60 ft. without armor","maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+3 axiomatic keen scythe +35 (2d4+19/19-20/x4) or fear touch +31 (fear)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fear touch","details":"Will DC 27, fear spell, CL 20th"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":28,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"fire shield"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"circle of death"},{"spell":"flesh to stone"},{"spell":"symbol of pain"},{"spell":"symbol of sleep"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 nupperibos, 2d6 bearded devils, bone devils or erinyes, or 1 ghaddar 100%"}]}],"strength":33,"dexterity":25,"constitution":27,"intelligence":26,"wisdom":26,"charisma":25,"baseatk":20,"cmb":31,"cmd":55,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (scythe)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":28},{"skill":"Bluff","value":30},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":30},{"skill":"Disguise","value":27},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":30},{"skill":"Fly","value":34},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":35},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":35},{"skill":"Stealth","value":30},{"skill":"Survival","value":28}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Infernal","Terran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Baaphel plus 2-5 bearded devils, 1-2 barbed devils, or 1 pit fiend)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This dog-headed humanoid has grayish-brown, pale scarlet eyes, and two upright crimson horns. Two, large, black bat-like wings sprout from its shoulders. Its hands are clawed and its feet are blackened hooves. A forked crimson tail snakes behind it.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fear Touch","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by Baaphel's fear touch for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based. Hell's Gleaning: Baaphel's unique weapon is a +3 axiomatic keen scythe."}],"description":"Baaphel is a grand duke in the service of Belial, leading 2 legions of bearded devils in battle for his lord. Baaphel is constantly scheming against the other dukes in Belial's service and takes every opportunity to discredit them in the eyes of their lord, though he never does this openly; it is always through lesser dukes and other devils that his machinations come to fruition. Baaphel yearns to be ruler of an entire plane and is waiting anxiously until the time comes that he can overthrow his lord.\n\nBaaphel makes his home in a great castle of basalt and iron called Evermore on Hell's fourth plane.\n\nBaaphel stands 7 ft. tall and weighs about 400 pounds.\n\nBaaphel attacks with Hell's Gleaning and spell-like abilities. He usually opens combat with flesh to stone, taking out the most able bodied attackers.\n\nBaaphel wears +3 chainmail and is rarely encountered without it.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"Hell's Gleaning, +3 chainmail"},{"name":"Maphistal (Second of Orcus)","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["unholy aura (DC 26)"],"ac":39,"ac_touch":24,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +15 natural, -1 size, +8 profane","hp":330,"hd":"20d10+220","hdvalue":20,"fort":25,"ref":13,"will":21,"dr":"20/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":32,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":80,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+3 unholy crushing heavy mace +35 (2d6+16 plus bone knit) or 2 claws +32 (1d6+13), bite +32 (1d8+13 plus disease)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":31,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"create undead"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"power word stun"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"telekinesis"},{"spell":"tongues","details":"self only"},{"spell":"unhallow"},{"spell":"unholy blight"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"circle of death"},{"spell":"fire storm"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 dretches, 1d4 hezrous, 1 nalfeshnee, 1 glabrezu, 1 marilith, or 1 balor 100%"},{"spell":"summon undead","details":"level 9, 3d10 zombies or skeletons, 2d6 ghouls, 2d4 ghasts, 1d6 wraiths, 1d6 wights, or 1d4 spectres 100%"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"create greater undead"}]}],"strength":36,"dexterity":25,"constitution":33,"intelligence":25,"wisdom":25,"charisma":26,"baseatk":20,"cmb":34,"cmd":59,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":35},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":31},{"skill":"Disguise","value":32},{"skill":"Fly","value":32},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (nobility)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":42},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":34},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":30},{"skill":"Stealth","value":26},{"skill":"Use Magical Device","value":31}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Ignan","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Maphistal plus 2-16 skeletons and zombies and 1-4 wights or 1-4 spectres and 1-8 wraiths)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"A stinking aura of death and decay lingers in the air around this feral-looking humanoid. Two great horns protrude upward from its oval head.  Huge leathery, bat-like wings sprout from its shoulders, and its lower torso sports two massive legs that end in soot-colored hooves. Short, coarse black hair covers its entire body, except its face and clawed hands.","group":"Demon Lord","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Bone Knit","kind":"Su","details":"Each time a living creature is hit by a weapon wielded by Maphistal, it must succeed on a DC 25 Fortitude save or take 1d4 points of Dexterity damage as its bones fuse together. Creatures without bones or skeletal structures (such as oozes and plants) are immune to this effect."},{"type":"Disease","kind":"Ex","details":"Demon Fever: Bite-injury; save Fort DC 31; onset 1day, frequency 1 day, effect 1d6 Con damage and target must make a second Fort save or 1 point of the damage is Con drain instead, cure 2 consecutive saves. Vox: Maphistal's unique weapon is a +3 unholy crushing heavy mace. The crushing special quality crushes the skulls of those it strikes. Upon a successful critical hit, the weapon crushes the opponent's skull (if it has one) instantly killing the target. Some creatures, such as many aberrations and all oozes, have no skulls, others, such as golems and incorporeal undead, are not affected by the crushing special quality. Most other creatures, however, die when their skull is crushed."}],"description":"Maphistal is a lieutenant in the employ of Orcus, Demon Prince of the Undead. He makes his home on a stinking, smoldering Abyssal plane where he commands his troops from his great castle, Maalstege (The Keep of Bones-so called because it is believed to be constructed from the skeletal remains of those slain by Maphistal). He is loyal to no one but Orcus. He doesn't trust Sonechard, the General of Orcus's undead legions, and seeks to discredit him at any opportunity, though he doesn't do this openly for fear of rebellion by his troops or punishment by Orcus.\n\nHis machinations against Sonechard are primarily through his agents and spies in Sonechard's camps.\n\nMaphistal stands 9 ft. tall and weighs 700 pounds.\n\nMaphistal is rarely, if ever, encountered alone, and usually has a retinue of undead with him. When he enters combat, he usually opens with his spell-like abilities, immediately using his circle of death ability to affect as many targets as possible. In melee, he batters an opponent with his mace. An opponent whose skull is destroy (and who is therefore slain) or an opponent brought to Dexterity 0 (and not rescued by his comrades) is carried back to the Keep of Bones where it is transformed into an undead creature or becomes part of the Keep itself.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Maphistal first appeared in the Necromancer Games module R3 Rappan Athuk 3: The Lower Levels (©2002, Necromancer Games, Inc.).","gear":"Vox"},{"name":"Sonechard (General of Orcus)","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["unholy aura (DC 27)","stench (20 ft., DC 32, nauseated, 10 rounds)"],"ac":46,"ac_touch":24,"ac_flat_footed":40,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +22 natural, -1 size, +9 profane","hp":385,"hd":"22d10+264","hdvalue":22,"fort":25,"ref":13,"will":21,"dr":"20/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":32,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":80,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+4 unholy wounding heavy pick +39 (1d8+17/19-20/x4 plus 1 bleed) or 2 claws +34 (1d8+13)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"control undead"},{"type":"undead master"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":32,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"create undead"},{"spell":"death knell"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"power word stun"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"telekinesis"},{"spell":"tongues","details":"self only"},{"spell":"unhallow"},{"spell":"unholy blight"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"circle of death"},{"spell":"destruction"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 dretches, 1d4 hezrous, or 1 nalfeshnee, 1 glabrezu, 1 marilith, or 1 balor 100%"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 zombies or skeletons, 2d8 shadows, wights, or wraiths, 2d4 greater shadows or spectres, or 1d4 dread wraiths 100%"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"create greater undead"},{"spell":"fireball"}]}],"strength":37,"dexterity":23,"constitution":34,"intelligence":26,"wisdom":26,"charisma":28,"baseatk":22,"cmb":36,"cmd":61,"feats":[{"feat":"Bleeding Critical"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (heavy pick)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (heavy pick)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":17},{"skill":"Bluff","value":38},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":34},{"skill":"Disguise","value":35},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":28},{"skill":"Fly","value":22},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":34},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (nobility)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Perception","value":41},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":33},{"skill":"Stealth","value":27},{"skill":"Survival","value":33}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Ignan","Infernal","Terran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Sonechard plus 1-4 wraiths or spectres, 2-16 shadows and 2-20 skeletons or zombies)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This ram-headed humanoid appears to be at least as twice as tall as a human and has leathery gray skin. Large, curved horns,-the left one broken off midway from its starting point-jut from its head. Two large bat-like wings spread from his shoulders. The creature's body is covered in thick, dark hair. Portions of the hair are torn away in areas revealing masses of battle-born scars and damage.","group":"Demon Lord","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Control Undead","kind":"Su","details":"This ability functions as the spell of the same name (CL 20th), except that Sonechard maintains control for 200 minutes. Sonechard can take control of undead creatures controlled by another creature whose caster level is 19 or less by making a successful opposed Charisma check against the opponent's Charisma check."},{"type":"Undead Master","kind":"Ex","details":"This ability allows Sonechard to create a maximum of 50 HD of undead with a single use of animate dead. If used in conjunction with desecrate, he can create 100 HD of undead with a single use. Fool's Errand: Sonechard's unique weapon is a +4 unholy wounding heavy pick."}],"description":"Sonechard is a General in the infernal armies of Orcus and serves him—at least to all onlookers—with unswerving loyalty. He has countless numbers of demons and undead at his command. Though his true loyalty lies only to himself, he would never openly refuse a request by Orcus nor challenge his position as Prince of the Undead. Should the day come when Orcus weakens, Sonechard plans to be there to claim what he believes is rightfully his.\n\nSonechard makes his home in a large castle called Chillhall that sits atop a plateau of scorched earth surrounded by a moat of blood. The walls are constructed of bone and sinew, and it is said that the souls of those who cross him are entombed within.\n\nSonechard stands 14 ft. tall and weighs about 3,500 pounds.\n\nSonechard is almost always encountered with a large number of demons or undead at his side. When he enters battle, he usually unleashes a fireball at his foes immediately, and then follows it up with a circle of death effect or a suggestion. Dying creatures are subjected to his death knell spell-like ability and then raised via animate dead.\n\nShould Sonechard find himself on the losing end of a battle, he doesn't hesitate to retreat, covering his escape with summoned or created undead and demons. A defeat isn't forgotten-or forgiven. He remembers his opponents, and sends his troops to exterminate them at first chance, bringing their carcasses to his keep where he grinds their remains into a fine powder and gives it to his servants to be used to spice up the keep's foodstuffs.\n\nSonechard's natural weapons, as well as any weapons he wields, are treated as chaotic-aligned and evil-aligned for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"Fool's Errand"},{"name":"Stygian Leviathan","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Colossal","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["aquatic","extraplanar"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":28,"ac_touch":3,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +25 natural, -8 size","hp":522,"hd":"36d10+324","hdvalue":36,"fort":31,"ref":23,"will":16,"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +45 (4d6+24/19-20/x2 plus grab)","space":"70 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"capsize"},{"type":"Stygian poisoning"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"4d6+24 plus 2d6 acid plus Stygian poisoning, AC 22, hp 52"}],"strength":43,"dexterity":13,"constitution":28,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":14,"charisma":6,"baseatk":36,"cmb":60,"cmd":71,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Overrun"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Staggering Critical"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":29},{"skill":"Swim","value":45}],"languages":["Common (cannot speak)"],"environments":["any (River Styx)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A gigantic whale, twice the size of ship surfaces. Its dark gray flesh contrasts hideously with the yellowish-white of its underbelly. It cuts through the water with a short, gray-mottled gray dorsal fin with a sharp curve. Its enormous mouth is lined with nearly 600 teeth of white or pale ivory color.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Capsize","kind":"Ex","details":"A Stygian leviathan can attempt to capsize a boat or ship by ramming it as a charge attack and making a CMB check. The DC of this check is 25, or the result of the captain's Profession (sailor) check, whichever is higher. For each size category the ship is larger than the leviathan's size, the leviathan takes a cumulative -10 penalty on this CMB check."},{"type":"Stygian Poisoning","kind":"Su","details":"The Stygian leviathan's stomach contains large quantities of water from the River Styx. Each round a swallowed opponent must succeed at a DC Swim or the swallowed creature slips underwater. Thereafter they must make a successful DC Fortitude save each round or be affected as by a feeblemind spell."}],"description":"The Stygian leviathan is the largest known creature swimming the River Styx. Very few inhabitants bother this monster and it has no known natural enemies.\n\nIt spends its time swimming throughout the Styx, gulping massive quantities of Stygian plants and aquatic life (such as fiendish octopi and fiendish krakens). Occasionally, it slips through a portal that leads to other planes-most often these portals carry it to the Material Plane. On the Material Plane, the Stygian leviathan doesn't deviate from its course-it simply swims about devouring whatever happens to get in its way. Some, on the other hand, actively hunt aquatic animals, preferring their flesh to the other more mundane food these monsters usually consume.\n\nThese beasts are solitary creatures and no more than a single leviathan has ever been encountered at one time (thankfully). Mating and reproduction cycles and methods are unknown and have never been documented.\n\nThese monsters are hunted by demons and devils for their flesh, which is used for food. Also, the teeth of dead Stygian leviathans are sometimes taken and fashioned into weapons of war.\n\nA Stygian leviathan attacks by simply swimming over its foes, opening its mouth, and swallowing them (and perhaps their ship if such a vessel is involved). Swallowed foes are drowned and digested.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Vepar (Duke of Dagon)","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["aquatic","chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":12,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["unholy aura (DC 27)"],"ac":37,"ac_touch":26,"ac_flat_footed":29,"ac_mods":"+8 Dex, +11 natural, -1 size, +9 profane","hp":363,"hd":"22d10+242","hdvalue":22,"fort":26,"ref":21,"will":15,"dr":"15/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":32,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"+2 trident +35 (2d6+13/19-20) or 2 claws +33 (1d8+11 plus hypothermic touch)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":31,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"control water"},{"spell":"control weather"},{"spell":"control winds"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect law"},{"spell":"fear"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"polymorph","details":"self only"},{"spell":"water breathing","details":"others only"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"ice storm"},{"spell":"implosion"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 2d6 shrroths, 1d4 hezrous, 1d2 nalfeshnees or mariliths, or 1 balor 100%"}]}],"strength":33,"dexterity":26,"constitution":33,"intelligence":27,"wisdom":27,"charisma":29,"baseatk":22,"cmb":34,"cmd":61,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (trident)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (ice storm)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (trident)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":38},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":31},{"skill":"Disguise","value":35},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":30},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":45},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":37},{"skill":"Stealth","value":29},{"skill":"Survival","value":30},{"skill":"Swim","value":22},{"skill":"Use Magical Device","value":31}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aquan","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Infernal","Undercommon","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"}],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Vepar plus 2-5 shrroths)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature appears as a giant-sized merman with coppery-brown skin and silver scales. Its long black hair is braided and it carries a menacing-looking trident.","group":"Demon Lord","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Hypothermic Touch","kind":"Ex","details":"Those hit by Vepar's claw attack must make a successful DC 32 Fortitude save or be overcome with bone-numbing cold that deals 1d8 points of Dexterity damage. A successful save reduces the ability score damage by half. The save DC is Constitution-based. Demonbrand: Vepar's unique weapon is a Large +2 trident that can cast magic missiles seven times per day as a swift action (CL 15th). Additionally, the wielder can cast waves of fatigue once per day (CL 15th)."}],"description":"Vepar is an Abyssal duke in the service of Dagon, Prince of the Sea. He leads 29 battalions of shrroths in service to his master. He is a brooding particularly mortals (whose very existence he disdains). His loyalty to Dagon is questionable at best, for behind the scenes, Vepar is quietly amassing an army of demons to one day lead against his current lord. But for now, he waits and serves.\n\nVepar's citadel, Leviathan's Reach, is built into an underwater mountain range that sits several miles below the surface of his watery Abyssal home.\n\nThe citadel is guarded by scores of aquatic demons, fiendish merfolk, and fiendish tritons, as well as several hundred sahuagin led by a fiendish sahuagin 15th-level sorcerer named Anaunon. Most visitors (those that can actually reach it) avoid this place.\n\nVepar resembles a 12-foot tall merman. His upper torso is copperybrown while his lower torso and fins are silver and scaled. Vepar's hair is long and black, and he usually wears it tied back or braided. His eyes, usually blue in color, burn with a silvery fire when he is angered or excited. Under his hair, two small copper horns can be seen just above his eyes. Vepar's hands end in wicked claws with silvery nails.\n\nVepar relies on his trident, spell-like abilities, and ability to deal ability damage when combating foes. Before entering combat, he often raises a storm (using control weather or control winds) to herald his coming, though he is just as likely to attack from ambush or surprise as he is to \"announce\" his arrival. He enters combat with unholy aura active and follows it closely with ice storm.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"Demonbrand"},{"name":"Baal (Duke of Hell)","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see invisibility"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"auras":["fear (20 ft., Will DC 29)"],"ac":38,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":36,"ac_mods":"+9 armor, +2 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size, +8 profane","hp":333,"hd":"23d10+207","hdvalue":23,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":16,"ref":20,"will":22,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":33,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30,"special":"40 ft. without armor"}],"melee":"+4 unholy morningstar +40 (2d6+17/19-20)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (20 ft. with morningstar)","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":29,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"comprehend languages"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"disguise self"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"inflict serious wounds"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"produce flame"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"unhallow"},{"spell":"unholy aura"},{"spell":"wall of fire"},{"spell":"wind walk"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"fire storm"},{"spell":"symbol of stunning"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"shapechange"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 lemures or nupperibos, 2d4 barbed devils, bearded devils, or gorgons, 1d4 erinyes, or 1 ghaddar devil, horned devil, or pit fiend 100%"}]}],"strength":37,"dexterity":25,"constitution":29,"intelligence":25,"wisdom":25,"charisma":27,"baseatk":23,"cmb":37,"cmd":62,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (morningstar)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (morningstar)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":34},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":34},{"skill":"Disguise","value":34},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":26},{"skill":"Fly","value":24},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":34},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":33},{"skill":"Perception","value":37},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":37},{"skill":"Stealth","value":25},{"skill":"Survival","value":30}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Daemonic"],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Baal plus 2-5 horned devils or 2-4 barbed devils)"],"treasure":"double standard Sheol: Baal's unique weapon is a Large +4 unholy morningstar. As a free action, the handle of Baal's morningstar can extend 10 ft., thus increasing his reach with this weapon. It can likewise retract to its normal length as a free action.","description_visual":"This diabolical-looking golden-skinned humanoid towers over you, dressed in battered bronze chainmail. It wields a large morningstar in its clawed hand as it stares at you. Its bovine head features large round eyes of black, a large nose, wolf-like upright ears, and a large mouth lined with razor-sharp teeth. Tiny forward-curving horns protrude from its forehead.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"Baal is a duke in the employ of Great Mammon and leads 5 legions of barbed devils in his service. Baal follows Lord Mammon's orders without question but secretly plans one day to wrest the throne from his master (who has become complacent as of late). For now, though, he waits and schemes.\n\nBaal stands 8 ft. tall and weighs 500 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Baal originally appeared as \"Bael\" in Dragon #75 (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission.","gear":"Sheol, +3 chainmail"},{"name":"Cherum","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Colossal","type":"aberration","subtypes":["fire"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."}],"auras":["fiery aura (40 ft., 6d6 fire, DC 36)"],"ac":37,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +1 dodge, +30 natural, -8 size","hp":450,"hd":"36d8+288","hdvalue":36,"hp_mods":["fast healing 15 when touching fire"],"fort":22,"ref":18,"will":24,"dr":"15/epic","immunities":["fire","poison"],"sr":33,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +33 (4d8+14/19-20 plus 2d6 fire plus grab), 2  claws +33 (3d6+14/19-20 plus 2d6 fire)","space":"30 ft.","reach":"30 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"swallow whole","details":"3d6+14 plus 2d6 fire damage, AC 25, 45 hp"}],"strength":39,"dexterity":18,"constitution":26,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":14,"charisma":12,"baseatk":27,"cmb":49,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. bull rush, grapple","cmd":64,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. bull rush","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite, claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":53},{"skill":"Bluff","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":54},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":22},{"skill":"Perception","value":45},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24},{"skill":"Survival","value":23}],"languages":["Common","Giant"],"environments":["warm mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double","description_visual":"This hairless mountain of slick raw burning flesh seems to constantly sizzle and ooze with the stench of burning fat. Two long meaty arms sprout from a hugely obese frame; its head appears to be little more than a bald sloping brow with black pits for eyes. Its maw splits open to reveal cavernous jaws, teeth glowing like huge red hot coals.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fast Healing","kind":"Ex","details":"A cherum heals only if it is touching a flame or lava pool that covers at least an area equal to its space (30-foot area)."}],"description":"The cherum is an abomination born of intense heat and crushing despair. Often making their homes in lava sprues, they are thought to be the rejected offspring of a fire deity (or at least the creation of said deity).\n\nAs such, they are often worshipped as divine beings by primitive folk who offer virgin sacrifices to appease the \"God of the Mountain.\" The cherum greedily devours such gifts, demanding more and more delicate flesh to feed its insatiable appetite. A cherum's deific background subjects it to fits of rage that can be felt for miles (especially when the cherum goes on a rampage and destroys the countryside).\n\nThough neutral by nature, cherum are often on decent terms with fire giants and other fire-based creatures that dwell near them. Though they don't trade with such creatures and rarely, if ever, aid them in time of need, they don't usually attack or demand homage from said creatures either. Cherum don't associate with dragons of any sort, especially red dragons for whom they have a great hatred.\n\nA cherum stands about 70 ft. tall and weighs well over 40,000 pounds.\n\nCherum are known to climb from a pool of molten magma, stretch forth their massive arms and devour everything in their grasp. They have little fear of dragons, demons, devils, or foolish adventurers who wander too close to their lair. They seek to grab and swallow everything smaller than themselves. If a fight goes against a cherum, it attempts to flee by diving into the nearest pool of lava and wait for its aggressors to leave as it heals.\n\nShould this fail, it fights on to the death.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Deep Hunter Sea Serpent","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"LN","size":"Gargantuan","type":"dragon","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +1 dodge, +12 natural, -4 size","hp":324,"hd":"24d12+168","hdvalue":24,"fort":23,"ref":15,"will":12,"immunities":["paralysis and sleep","dragon traits"],"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +31 (2d8+15/19-20 plus poison and grab)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"2d8+15"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"2d8+15 bludgeoning plus 1d8 acid damage, AC 15, 25 hp"}],"strength":31,"dexterity":13,"constitution":24,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":13,"charisma":12,"baseatk":24,"cmb":41,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":57,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Bleeding Critical"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Armor"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Swim-By Attack","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":13},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":14},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":24},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16},{"skill":"Survival","value":28},{"skill":"Swim","value":38}],"languages":["Aquan","Draconic"],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"The serpent is about 60 ft. long and 10 ft. thick. Its body scales are smooth, each about the size of a large shield, and the entire serpent is deep green to jet black in color, with eyes a solid, nearly black red color.","group":"Sea Serpent","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 29; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d6 Str; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"The immense deep hunter serpent lives in deep oceans, and delights in hunting down and killing the most fearsome creatures of the sea. The deep hunter lives on the ocean floor, usually near thermal vents and volcanic areas where it is relatively warm. However, when hunting it may be encountered just about anywhere at sea; its preferred prey are krakens and the largest whales, though it may attack any other fearsome sea predator-the more dangerous, the better.\n\nThe deep hunter sea serpent is seldom seen near the surface, as its prey tends to stick to deep waters. It doesn't initiate combat against creatures it sees as its inferiors, but if it does regard a creature as a threat, it uses stealth to surprise its prey when possible, and launches into a full-scale assault using all of its physical attacks to the best of its ability.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Elemental Fire Dragon","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","fire"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["fiery aura (60 ft., DC 27, 2d8 fire)"],"ac":30,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +16 natural, -2 size","hp":252,"hd":"24d10+120","hdvalue":24,"fort":13,"ref":20,"will":16,"dr":"10/epic and silver","immunities":["elemental traits","fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +32 (2d8+13 plus burn), 2 claws +32 (2d6+9 plus burn), 2 wings +29 (1d8+9 plus burn), tail slap +29 (2d6+13 plus burn)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50 ft. cone, DC 29, 16d10 fire"},{"type":"burn","details":"2d8, DC 27 rain of fire (100 ft. radius, DC 27, 2d8 fire)"}],"strength":28,"dexterity":23,"constitution":21,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":12,"baseatk":24,"cmb":35,"cmd":51,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (breath weapon)"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":25},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":29},{"skill":"Survival","value":29}],"languages":["Common","Ignan"],"environments":["any (Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature appears as a 30-foot long dragon composed of fire. Its eyes burn with a white-hot flame and flames lick the dragon's great mouth as it roars. As it flies overhead, its wings send sheets of flame roaring into the sky and crashing into the ground.","group":"Elemental Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"Afire elemental dragon's breath weapon is a 50 ft. cone of elemental fire."},{"type":"Fiery Aura","kind":"Ex","details":"Anyone within 60 ft. of an elemental fire dragon must succeed on a DC 27 Fortitude save or take 2d8 points of fire damage from the intense heat. The save DC is Constitution-based. Combustibles automatically catch fire if they contact an elemental fire dragon."},{"type":"Rain of Fire","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, a hovering elemental fire dragon can rapidly beat its wings causing fire to rain down on an area in a 100-foot radius. Creatures within the area must succeed on a DC 27 Reflex save or take 2d8 points of fire damage as clothes catch fire or armor and weapons become searing hot. The damage continues for another 1d8 rounds after the attack or until the flames are extinguished. Combustibles in the area automatically catch on fire."}],"description":"One of the most feared creatures from the Plane of Fire is the dreaded elemental fire dragon. They make their homes in the heart of the many volcanoes that dot the elemental landscape. Composed entirely of flames, these magnificent creatures fear little and are respected and feared by those that have encountered them. Elemental fire dragons are malign, vicious, and thoroughly evil. They delight in killing and torturing others, especially magmin (whom they relish as a delicacy). They often employ salamanders to aid them in their adventures, but once they have accomplished their goals, any surviving salamanders are usually devoured. Elemental fire dragons cannot enter water or any other nonflammable liquid, but they can fly or step over it. The typical elemental fire dragon is at least 30 ft. long. Elemental fire dragons are ruthless adversaries. They care nothing for treasure or anything of value. An elemental fire dragon attempts to annihilate its opponents using any means possible.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Euryale","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":41,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":38,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +29 natural, -1 size","hp":270,"hd":"20d10+160","hdvalue":20,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":14,"ref":17,"will":19,"dr":"15/epic and good","immunities":["paralysis","polymorph","sleep","stunning"],"sr":33,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"2 claws +32 (2d6+12 plus grab), bite +32 (1d10+12),  snake bite +30 (1d8+6 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"petrifying gaze"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 2d6+18"}],"strength":35,"dexterity":17,"constitution":26,"intelligence":24,"wisdom":24,"charisma":28,"baseatk":20,"cmb":33,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":46,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (snake bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":26},{"skill":"Bluff","value":32},{"skill":"Craft (alchemy)","value":30},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":32},{"skill":"Fly","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":32},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":30},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":30},{"skill":"Stealth","value":22},{"skill":"Survival","value":27}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aklo","Common","Draconic","Infernal","Terran (Euryale only)","Undercommon"],"sq":[{"type":"immortal"}],"environments":["any (Outer Planes)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair (Sthenno and Euryale)","troupe (true gorgon plus 2-8 medusa and 1-4 greater medusa)"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"This hideous creature appears to be almost twice as tall as a normal human.  Its upper torso is that of a well proportioned human female with scaly flesh while its lower torso is that of a great black-scaled snake. Small black wings protrude from its back. Instead of hair, its head is covered with writhing, deadly asps. Its mouth is filled with razor-sharpened fangs.","group":"True Gorgon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Immortal","kind":"Ex","details":"Sthenno and Euryale are immortal and cannot die from natural causes. They are not subject to death from massive damage and are immune to death effects and disintegration. They don't age, and don't need to sleep, eat, or breathe."},{"type":"Petrifying Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Turn to stone permanently, 30 ft., Fortitude save (DC 27 Sthenno, DC 29 Euryale) negates. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 26 (Sthenno) or DC 28 (Euryale); frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d6 Strength; cure 1 save."}],"description":"Though the word gorgon is often associated with the deadly bull-like creature that turns a victim to stone with its breath weapon, the true gorgons are three sisters; Euryale, Sthenno, and Medusa. They are the daughters of the god Phorcys and the goddess Ceto. Euryale and Sthenno were born immortal and are hideous creatures with writing snakes for hair, brass claws, wings, and a gaze that can turn any living creature into stone. Phorcys tasked them with guarding the entrance to the Underworld.\n\nMedusa was born mortal and was very beautiful. Phorcys sent her to the Material Plane so all could gaze upon the beauty of his daughter.\n\nMedusa's beauty rivaled that of some of the goddesses, and some of them grew jealous of Medusa, particularly the goddess Athena. Her beauty also turned the heads of some of the gods, and when Poseidon seduced her in a temple to Athena, the goddess became enraged and changed the beautiful Medusa into a creature as hideous as her sisters. Poseidon turned from his love, never to return again. Medusa, enraged, fled into the desert and never came back to civilization.\n\nThe hero Perseus was tasked with killing the gorgon known as Medusa and bringing her head to King Polydectes as a wedding present. Using a magic shield given to him by the gods, he avoided Medusa's deadly gaze and severed her head. From her serpentine body sprang the children of Poseidon, creatures similar in appearance to their mother. These creatures escaped into the world and are called medusa.\n\nSthenno and Euryale long for their sister's return or their meeting with her in the Underworld. Yet being immortal, they cannot enter the Realm of the Dead. Thus, both know they will never see their beloved sibling again. Their cries are said to be audible on the wind as a high-pitched shrill akin to a bird's cry.\n\nBoth Sthenno and Euryale are 10 ft. tall and weigh around 600 pounds or more. Sthenno's eyes are blue; Euryale's eyes are copper.\n\nSthenno and Euryale rarely enter combat unless pressed or provoked.\n\nThey are both deadly combatants and use their claws, bite, snakes, and petrifying gaze with precision force. Sthenno enjoys \"collecting\" those she has turned to stone and even has a room in her lair where she displays them. Euryale simply smashes to rubble those she has petrified.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""}];
